# const_ns_qualified_visibility_rejected.tkr — a NAMESPACE-IDENTITY project-regressor (0.3.1
# regressor-principal, §5 triage exception): a `private` module-level const's visibility is
# gated by its DECLARING namespace, not the reference's. Needs a real second namespace (`m1`)
# distinct from the root; flattening would collapse the boundary under test. Kept on disk,
# unflattened; not inline-scenario-izable.

Feature: const_ns_qualified_visibility_rejected — private module-level const does not leak across a namespace-qualified reference

  Scenario: the root namespace may not read another namespace's private const, even namespace-qualified
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "is private to"
